   "result": "I added the 3D map as a new section at the top of `index.html`. Each station has a 승차 bar and a 하차 bar, and moving the time slider changes their heights to that hour's values. I loaded it in headless Chrome: no script errors, and the 08시 bars match the data. The old line charts and table are unchanged. I haven't tested dragging the slider, the ▶ button, or the hover tooltip, so check those in a real browser.\n\n**What's on the page:**\n- **Placement:** The stations sit where they really are relative to each other, from 서울역 to 종로5가, on a floor grid with name labels. The data file has no coordinates, so I typed in each station's latitude and longitude by hand.\n- **Bars:** Blue is 승차 and orange is 하차, the same colors as the existing legend. Every hour uses the same height scale, so you can compare bars across hours.\n- **Slider:** It runs from 04시 to 03시 the next day and starts at 08시. Heights change smoothly when you move it. The ▶ button steps forward one hour at a time and starts over after 03시.\n- **Tooltip:** Hovering a bar shows that station's 승차 and 하차 counts for the selected hour.\n- **Camera:** Drag to rotate, scroll to zoom.\n\n**One correction to the plan:** I said 서울역 하차 would be the tallest bar at 08시. In the data, 종각 하차 is a bit higher (285,007 vs 274,196), and the bars show that correctly.\n\nTo open it: run `python3 -m http.server 8000` in this folder, then go to http://127.0.0.1:8000. Opening the file directly won't load the data.",
